 "governance": {
  "change_controller": "The MCL maintainer (the owner of the eight MCL repositories).",
  "procedures": "mcl-core/governance/GOVERNANCE.md section 4 defines application, review, promotion and deprecation for every MCL registry. They are defined once there rather than restated per registry, so they cannot drift apart.",
  "application": "GOVERNANCE.md 4.1 -- an issue naming the registry, requested range, meaning, a permanent specification reference, and the failure behaviour required of a receiver that does not implement it. An application without a specification reference is not an application.",
  "review": "GOVERNANCE.md 4.2",
  "promotion": "GOVERNANCE.md 4.3 -- an Experimental Use value is NEVER relabelled Stable. Promotion assigns a NEW value in the Standards Action range after an independent implementation has interoperated using the experimental one, and re-runs conformance evidence on the final assigned bytes.",
  "deprecation": "GOVERNANCE.md 4.4 -- a retired assignment becomes a permanent tombstone. Its value is never reused and a decoder must refuse it, because a peer that once meant something by that value would otherwise be misread rather than refused."
 }
